==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brah Cats''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Val Val Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
The Bean Cats are quite fragile, so keep them protected whenever possible. They can be used to knockback Reds while your heavy attackers ([[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], etc.) deal with other threats. The Bean Cats are made obsolete by [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], since Pirate Cat has longer range, a shorter interval between attacks, a shorter recharge time and 10% more knockback chance in [[True Form]], which makes him more effective and easier to stack. Also, he only costs 15¢ more by Chapter 2 standards. The two of them can be used together if Pirate isn't enough alone.

Even for players without Pirate Cat, they can usually be replaced by [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] for stalling Reds, along with other units who are significantly better. However, they are included in [[Team of Two (Combo)|Team of Two]], a Unit Defense Up M [[Cat Combo|Combo]] which also contains [[Bouncing Four (Combo)|Bouncing Four]] and [[Double Date (Combo)|Double Date]].

==='''True Form'''===
Their true form gains several buffs, including increased defense, the Resistant ability, a guaranteed level-1 wave, and Behemoth Slayer.

The increased defense and resistance helps this unit become a better anti-red, mainly in the early-game and mid-game. While this already breathes new life into these units, this mainly pairs with their 100% chance to generate a level 1 wave, giving them an effective area attack with a 30% chance to knock red enemies back while taking quite some damage from them. While this niche becomes less relevant in the end-game, this is still useful for how easily accessible it is in the early-game. In addition, their pseudo area attacks can make them more useful than Pirate Cat in many stages, as Pirate has trouble dealing with groups of Reds.

Another early-game and mid-game niche for this unit is also brought about by its Behemoth Slayer ability. Combining this ability with a resistance to Red and increased defense, this ability helps when dealing with one enemy in particular, [[Casaurian Ahirujo]]. In particular, this unit helps to tank with a decent dodge chance against this red duck and keep it back with pseudo area attacks. With how easily accessible this true form becomes, requiring a single red B.Stone, this unit is meant to handle Ahirujo and help the player acquire the powerful [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]].

However, once the player does get the B.Stones necessary to evolve Courier, then Val Val Cat becomes almost obsolete against Behemoths, though that speaks more to Courier's power. Courier is powerful against Red enemies in general, though early-game and mid-game players can use Courier alongside Val Val Cat in many stages. To add to this, Val Val Cat still has those useful Cat Combos.

Overall, while this unit is not overpowered, it received a satisfactory true form upgrade.

